From 5edd8f4545e1aca1f9e78376f4477b87ba4f81bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FVOCI <150913557+fvoci@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:46:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(collab): save a live state left without a room before
 moving its document (#71 review)

1. Without a room, a live state left pending by an earlier room (its last
   snapshot found no editor who could write, or the server stopped right
   after a periodic store) was moved as is. Those edits may already have
   been acknowledged; in a target workspace with realtime off nothing
   recovers them and the next normal save drops them. Rooms::move_document
   now, under the moving guard and before the move transaction, loads the
   document like save_pending and writes the stored state as a revision
   (existing author order, the mover stands in). It does nothing when no
   state is stored (the room would build from the body; no state row is
   created), when the state reads the same as the body written into Yjs
   (a room that only opened: the editor's null attributes do not survive
   Yjs, so a plain body comparison would add a revision on every move), or
   when realtime is off for the document (turning it off saves pending
   states first). If the revision cannot be written (no editor, error,
   timeout, changed outside) nothing is moved: 409 with the in-room
   checkpoint's messages, now shared by both paths.
2. The in-room move also checks that the caller is still waiting before
   the checkpoint, so a gone request does not write a checkpoint revision.
3. drain_after_move kept dropping a Shutdown that arrived after the commit;
   close_all reads a dropped answer as saved, so a realtime-off of the
   target workspace could run its pending scan before the moved room wrote
   its revision or stored its state. The room now keeps those answers and
   sends the post-commit snapshot result after the revision attempt and
   the store. No test: the race needs a second request to land in the
   microseconds between the commit and the drain, which cannot be forced
   without test-only hooks.
4. edits_held_by_a_move_that_does_not_happen_are_accepted no longer
   sleeps: after sending the edit the client pings and waits for the pong.
   The server reads frames in order and puts an edit into the room queue
   before reading the next frame, and tungstenite sends the pong on the
   read after the ping, so the pong proves the edit waits behind the held
   move. The test also checks it was not acknowledged while held.

Tests: a_move_without_a_room_saves_a_live_state_left_pending (fails
before: the acknowledged edit is not in the moved document), which also
checks that a document never opened gets no state row or revision and a
document whose room only opened gets no revision.

